==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|ang}} {{term|hæfen|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Germanic|xaƀanō}} (compare Dutch {{term|haven|lang=nl}}, German {{term|Hafen|lang=de}}, Danish/Norwegian {{term|havn|lang=da}}), from ''xaƀan'' 'sea' (compare Old English {{term|hæf|lang=ang}}, German {{term|Haff|lang=de}} 'gulf', Danish {{term|hav|lang=da}}), from {{proto|Indo-European|kopno}} (compare Irish {{term|cúan|lang=ga}} 'harbor, recess, haven'). See also ''[[hav]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈheɪvən/}}
* {{audio|En-us-haven.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|eɪvən}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[harbour]] or [[anchorage]] protected from the sea.
# {{context|by extension}} A place of [[safety]]; a refuge or sanctuary.

====Synonyms====
* [[refuge]]
* [[sanctuary]]
* [[zoar]]

====Derived terms====
* [[tax haven]]

